Absolutely — I interpreted this as a responsible-gambling app that helps users protect themselves from risky betting habits and manipulative casino UX, rather than anything deceptive or exploitative.

Here’s a solid MVP you can build.

Project concept: Gambling Guard
A mobile app that helps users:
- track spending and time spent gambling
- set limits and cool-downs
- detect risky patterns
- block impulsive deposits
- show a clear spending summary
- enforce breaks and safer play habits

Recommended stack
- Frontend: React Native + Expo
- Backend: Node.js + Express + TypeScript
- Database: PostgreSQL
- Auth: Firebase Auth or Clerk
- Notifications: Firebase Cloud Messaging
- Analytics: PostHog or Mixpanel

Project structure
- app/
  - src/
    - app/
      - auth/
      - dashboard/
      - limits/
      - sessions/
      - reports/
      - onboarding/
    - components/
    - hooks/
    - lib/
    - types/
    - services/
  - api/
    - src/
      - routes/
      - controllers/
      - db/
      - utils/
  - prisma/
    - schema.prisma

Core app features
- User onboarding
  - set daily/weekly loss limit
  - set time limit
  - choose risk alert preferences
- Session tracking
  - timer for active gambling sessions
  - deposit and loss tracking
  - suspicious pattern detection
- Cool-down / self-exclusion
  - 24h / 7d / 30d break options
  - forced pause after threshold crossed
- Risk scoring
  - examples:
    - loss > 60% of weekly limit
    - 3+ sessions in 24h
    - repeated “one more spin” behavior
- Weekly report
  - total time spent
  - total losses
  - highest-risk days
  - safe-play streak
- Notification engine
  - reminders at threshold
  - break prompts
  - self-exclusion reminders

Data model
Use PostgreSQL tables like:

users
- id
- email
- name
- created_at
- timezone
- onboarding_complete

limits
- id
- user_id
- daily_loss_limit
- weekly_loss_limit
- daily_time_limit_minutes
- session_cooldown_minutes
- created_at
- updated_at

sessions
- id
- user_id
- started_at
- ended_at
- duration_minutes
- total_bet_amount
- total_won_amount
- total_lost_amount
- source_type
- notes

deposits
- id
- user_id
- amount
- currency
- created_at
- source

alerts
- id
- user_id
- type
- severity
- message
- triggered_at
- resolved_at

self_exclusions
- id
- user_id
- start_at
- end_at
- reason
- active

risk_events
- id
- user_id
- event_type
- score_delta
- created_at

Example Prisma schema
```prisma
generator client {
  provider = "prisma-client-js"
}

datasource db {
  provider = "postgresql"
  url      = env("DATABASE_URL")
}

model User {
  id                  String   @id @default(cuid())
  email               String   @unique
  name                String?
  createdAt           DateTime @default(now())
  onboardingComplete  Boolean  @default(false)
  timezone            String?
  limits              Limit[]
  sessions            Session[]
  deposits            Deposit[]
  alerts              Alert[]
  exclusions          SelfExclusion[]
  riskEvents          RiskEvent[]
}

model Limit {
  id                    String   @id @default(cuid())
  userId                String
  dailyLossLimit        Float?
  weeklyLossLimit       Float?
  dailyTimeLimitMinutes Int?
  sessionCooldownMinutes Int?
  createdAt             DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt             DateTime @updatedAt

  user User @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id])
}

model Session {
  id              String   @id @default(cuid())
  userId          String
  startedAt       DateTime
  endedAt         DateTime?
  durationMinutes Int?
  totalBetAmount  Float   @default(0)
  totalWonAmount  Float   @default(0)
  totalLostAmount Float   @default(0)
  sourceType      String?
  notes           String?
  createdAt       DateTime @default(now())

  user User @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id])
}

model Deposit {
  id        String   @id @default(cuid())
  userId    String
  amount    Float
  currency  String
  createdAt DateTime @default(now())

  user User @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id])
}

model Alert {
  id          String   @id @default(cuid())
  userId      String
  type        String
  severity    String
  message     String
  triggeredAt DateTime @default(now())
  resolvedAt  DateTime?

  user User @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id])
}

model SelfExclusion {
  id        String   @id @default(cuid())
  userId    String
  startAt   DateTime
  endAt     DateTime
  reason    String?
  active    Boolean @default(true)

  user User @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id])
}

model RiskEvent {
  id          String   @id @default(cuid())
  userId      String
  eventType   String
  scoreDelta  Int
  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())

  user User @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id])
}
```

Backend API example
`api/src/routes/limits.ts`
```ts
import express from "express";
import { PrismaClient } from "@prisma/client";

const router = express.Router();
const prisma = new PrismaClient();

router.post("/limits", async (req, res) => {
  const {
    userId,
    dailyLossLimit,
    weeklyLossLimit,
    dailyTimeLimitMinutes,
    sessionCooldownMinutes
  } = req.body;

  const limit = await prisma.limit.create({
    data: {
      userId,
      dailyLossLimit,
      weeklyLossLimit,
      dailyTimeLimitMinutes,
      sessionCooldownMinutes
    }
  });

  res.json(limit);
});

router.get("/limits/:userId", async (req, res) => {
  const limit = await prisma.limit.findFirst({
    where: { userId: req.params.userId },
    orderBy: { createdAt: "desc" }
  });

  res.json(limit);
});

export default router;
```

Risk detection logic
Example function:
```ts
type RiskCheckInput = {
  dailyLoss: number;
  weeklyLoss: number;
  sessionCountToday: number;
  timeSpentMinutes: number;
  dailyLimit: number;
  weeklyLimit: number;
  dailyTimeLimit: number;
};

export function calculateRiskScore(input: RiskCheckInput): number {
  let score = 0;

  if (input.dailyLoss >= input.dailyLimit * 0.8) score += 25;
  if (input.weeklyLoss >= input.weeklyLimit * 0.7) score += 25;
  if (input.sessionCountToday >= 3) score += 20;
  if (input.timeSpentMinutes >= input.dailyTimeLimit * 0.8) score += 20;

  return Math.min(score, 100);
}
```

Example React Native screen
`App.tsx`
```tsx
import React, { useState } from "react";
import { View, Text, TextInput, Button, StyleSheet } from "react-native";

export default function App() {
  const [dailyLimit, setDailyLimit] = useState("100");
  const [weeklyLimit, setWeeklyLimit] = useState("400");
  const [timeLimit, setTimeLimit] = useState("90");

  const risk = calculateRiskScore({
    dailyLoss: 82,
    weeklyLoss: 310,
    sessionCountToday: 3,
    timeSpentMinutes: 78,
    dailyLimit: Number(dailyLimit),
    weeklyLimit: Number(weeklyLimit),
    dailyTimeLimit: Number(timeLimit),
  });

  return (
    <View style={styles.container}>
      <Text style={styles.title}>Gambling Guard</Text>

      <Text style={styles.label}>Daily loss limit</Text>
      <TextInput
        style={styles.input}
        value={dailyLimit}
        keyboardType="numeric"
        onChangeText={setDailyLimit}
      />

      <Text style={styles.label}>Weekly loss limit</Text>
      <TextInput
        style={styles.input}
        value={weeklyLimit}
        keyboardType="numeric"
        onChangeText={setWeeklyLimit}
      />

      <Text style={styles.label}>Daily time limit (minutes)</Text>
      <TextInput
        style={styles.input}
        value={timeLimit}
        keyboardType="numeric"
        onChangeText={setTimeLimit}
      />

      <Button title="Save limits" onPress={() => {}} />

      <View style={styles.riskBox}>
        <Text style={styles.riskText}>Risk score</Text>
        <Text style={styles.score}>{risk}/100</Text>
      </View>
    </View>
  );
}

function calculateRiskScore(input: {
  dailyLoss: number;
  weeklyLoss: number;
  sessionCountToday: number;
  timeSpentMinutes: number;
  dailyLimit: number;
  weeklyLimit: number;
  dailyTimeLimit: number;
}) {
  let score = 0;
  if (input.dailyLoss >= input.dailyLimit * 0.8) score += 25;
  if (input.weeklyLoss >= input.weeklyLimit * 0.7) score += 25;
  if (input.sessionCountToday >= 3) score += 20;
  if (input.timeSpentMinutes >= input.dailyTimeLimit * 0.8) score += 20;
  return Math.min(score, 100);
}

const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  container: {
    flex: 1,
    padding: 24,
    justifyContent: "center",
    backgroundColor: "#111827"
  },
  title: {
    fontSize: 28,
    fontWeight: "700",
    color: "#fff",
    marginBottom: 24
  },
  label: {
    color: "#d1d5db",
    marginBottom: 8
  },
  input: {
    backgroundColor: "#1f2937",
    color: "#fff",
    borderRadius: 10,
    padding: 12,
    marginBottom: 18
  },
  riskBox: {
    marginTop: 24,
    padding: 18,
    borderRadius: 12,
    backgroundColor: "#1d4ed8"
  },
  riskText: {
    color: "#dbeafe",
    fontSize: 14
  },
  score: {
    color: "#fff",
    fontSize: 32,
    fontWeight: "700"
  }
});
```

Suggested screens
- Onboarding
- Dashboard
- Limit settings
- Active session
- Weekly report
- Break / self-exclusion
- Alerts center

Example user flows
1. User signs up
2. Sets daily loss limit and time limit
3. App begins tracking sessions
4. If thresholds crossed:
   - show “You’ve reached 80% of your daily limit”
   - require confirmation before continuing
   - suggest a 15-minute break
5. If repeated:
   - trigger cool-down state
   - disable deposit actions until user opts in
6. Weekly summary:
   - “You spent 3h 20m and $420 this week. You hit 87% of your weekly limit.”

Best MVP features to prioritize
- limits
- session tracking
- risk alerts
- break screen
- weekly summary

